### **5. Sprint audit signals (sprint_audit.py:200-318)**

All thresholds are **CALIBRATION TARGETS (v0.6)**, not hard gates. See ADR 260601_sprint-audit-threshold-rationale.md.

| Signal | Threshold | Formula |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| **error_rate** | > 0.10 (10%) | error_count / total_all |
| **bypass_explicit** | > 0.30 (30%) | sidecar_mode='bypassed' AND agent_mode empty / total_all |
| **bypass_in_agent_mode** | > 0.05 (5%) | sidecar_mode='bypassed' AND agent_mode non-empty / agent_mode_runs |
| **outcome_entropy** | < 0.5 nats | Shannon entropy of outcome label distribution |
| **unfired_branches** | > 0.40 (40%) | (declared_outcomes - actual_outcomes) / declared_outcomes |
| **schema_overflow_rate** | (no hard threshold) | runs with metadata keys NOT in result_schema / runs_with_sidecar |
| **post_hoc_bias_flag** | worst_outcome > 10% in first 1/3 | Boolean flag (true if fail/error overrepresented early) |
| **premature_stopping_rate** | (no hard threshold) | sequential campaigns concluded below stopping_threshold / total_sequential_concluded |

